<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05MC">Remark <span data-tag="05MC">8.5.6.5</span>.</a> Let $\iota : \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 \hookrightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a monomorphism of simplicial sets and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ be an idempotent-complete $\infty $-category. If $\iota $ is a Morita equivalence, then the functor $\operatorname{Fun}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) \xrightarrow { \circ \iota } \operatorname{Fun}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}})$ is both an isofibration (Corollary <a data-tag="01F3" href="/tag/01F3">4.4.5.3</a>) and an equivalence of $\infty $-categories, and therefore a trivial Kan fibration (Proposition <a data-tag="01G7" href="/tag/01G7">4.5.6.20</a>). In particular, every diagram $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ can be extended to $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. </p>
